[{"code":"program_shape","severity":"error","span":{"file":"src/Main.beni","start":{"line":36,"col":31},"end":{"line":36,"col":46}},"title":"PROGRAM SHAPE","message":"A limit of the compiler: the schema a page's value is decoded with must be one\nthe compiler can see whole — a `schema` declaration's `Page.schema ⊤`,\n`Schema.derived ⊤`, or those composed by `Schema.list`, `Schema.nullable` and\n`Schema.converted`, written here or in a constant of this module — and this is a\nschema made when the program runs, or a value of another module the build does\nnot follow. A schema's conversions are values inside it that no walk of the\nprogram can read, so the build could not tell that decoding the value is pure\n(`docs/design/prerender.md` §8.4; `docs/design/browser-inline.md` §5, class 4).\nDeclare it with `schema`, and name it here."}]
